<div id="2026-09-10-3d-model-download-stale-nfs-path" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-10 — 3D model download error (stale nfs_path after NFS restructure)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Diagnosed auto-generated error todo (plan_rev: auto-error-audit) for <code>3d::model_download</code> "STL not visible at stored nfs_path=... resolved=&lt;empty&gt;". The failing model (HDRY Hydra Rollers, path containing 110520_HDRY_System_V3__AMS__Hydra__Rollers.3mf) and similar legacy project-import models store paths under the old <code>/data/nfs/3d/projects/hdry-v3/</code> location. <code>NfsPath::resolve_path</code> returns empty because <code>-f</code> fails; <code>model_download</code> logs at Controller/3d.pm:882 and redirects.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Pre-2026-08-25 project imports and early model records wrote absolute paths to then-current NFS layout. The restructure (portable Docker NFS volume, <code>fix_nfs_paths.sql</code>) moved files to <code>/data/nfs/hdry_parts/&lt;project&gt;/</code> (directories of .stl files, not .3mf) and updated only <code>nfs_directory</code> + <code>files</code> tables. <code>printing_3d_models.nfs_path</code> was untouched. New NfsPath resolution + error logging now surfaces the stale data. Same issue previously noted as "Still blocked" for model 16 in 2026-09-02 entry. The 2026-09-10 model_upload feature provides the correct remediation path (re-upload corrected STL).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/3d.pm:880</code> (model_download resolve + check), <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Util/NfsPath.pm</code> (resolve_path, to_container_path), <code>printing_3d_models</code> (stale rows), <code>fix_nfs_paths.sql</code> (incomplete migration), <code>.hermes/plans/2026-09-10-3d-model-download-stale-nfs-path.md</code> (full work order).</p>
</div>